GoldLink's change to melonDS (UC11): the field's camera for GoldLink. The position matrix the game
loads right after a field projection (world to view) goes with its scene through the swap to the
picture on screen (ShownCamera), with the world's shift on a picture in between
(ShownWorldShift): GoldLink finds where each pixel is in the world, and which map area it's in.

Applied by build.rs to a copy of the submodule (which stays at upstream).

--- a/src/GPU3D.h	2026-11-13 20:02:32.211219085 -0500
+++ b/src/GPU3D.h	2026-11-13 20:04:54.853381432 -0500
@@ -436,6 +436,16 @@
     bool MidPrepare() noexcept;
     void MidEndShown() noexcept;
 
+    // GoldLink (UC11): the field's camera (the position matrix loaded right after a field
+    // projection: world to view, 20.12, 4 rows of 3), for the scene being built, flushed,
+    // rendered and on screen; and how far the picture on screen has the world shifted (pixels,
+    // x then y: a picture in between draws its scene's world half a step back). GoldLink finds
+    // where each pixel is in the world with it (the lighting's neighbouring areas).
+    bool CameraNext = false;
+    s32 SceneCamera[12] {}, FlushedCamera[12] {}, RenderCamera[12] {}, ShownCamera[12] {};
+    bool SceneCameraSeen = false, FlushedCameraSeen = false, RenderCameraSeen = false, ShownCameraSeen = false;
+    s32 RenderWorldShift[2] {}, ShownWorldShift[2] {};
+
     u32 FlushRequest = 0;
     u32 FlushAttributes = 0;
     u32 ScrolledLine[256]; // not part of the hardware state, don't serialize
